# Answer-and-point cases (U10, kind "answer_point"). Scored offline by
# wisp/gauntlet.py (score_answer_point_cases), not by the sandbox driver, whose
# loader skips these rows. `reply` is a HAND-AUTHORED recorded model reply (not a
# model recording; same convention as scripts/gen_teach_fixtures.py). Points are
# raw-canvas screenshot px; expect_point.rect is in logical coords; the two
# monitor case also checks the monitor index. Public, generic content only.
# The pass-rate gate is not set here: it comes from the first owner-run live
# baseline (ANSWER_POINT_GATE in wisp/gauntlet.py).
